From: cef-patched
Subject: [PATCH] Use the system libffi instead of the static ffi_pic

TODO: USE GN_DEFINES
Chromium's Linux build normally links a static, position-independent
libffi (libffi_pic.a) provided by the sysroot. With use_sysroot=false the
build instead expects that archive from the host, which the FHS build
environment does not provide, so linking libvk_swiftshader.so fails with:

    mold: fatal: library not found: ffi_pic

Force use_system_libffi so the build resolves libffi through pkg-config
and links the shared library that the environment does provide.

diff --git a/build/config/linux/libffi/BUILD.gn b/build/config/linux/libffi/BUILD.gn
index 6e45f4c226..ecf83bff35 100644
--- a/build/config/linux/libffi/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/linux/libffi/BUILD.gn
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ declare_args() {
   # on Linux, libffi must be statically linked to prevent a situation where the
   # runtime version of libffi is different from the build-time version from the
   # sysroot.
-  use_system_libffi = default_toolchain == "//build/toolchain/cros:target"
+  use_system_libffi = true
 }
 
 if (use_system_libffi) {
